  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Forecast-based Preparedness Action (ForPAc): Probabilistic forecast information for defensible preparedness decision-making and action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of ForPAc is to enhance the ability of mandated agencies to undertake preparedness actions in advance of flood/drought hazard events, in Kenya and the Greater Horn of Africa (GHA). This will be done by addressing two primary limitations of existing flood and drought warning systems: firstly increasing the credibility and pertinence of hazard forecasts, by developing improved weather-climate forecasts and associated livelihood impacts over a range of &apos;seamless&apos; lead times from days to seasons; and secondly overcoming barriers to the implementation of risk reduction actions in advance of hazard events through the development and trialling of systematic approaches based on forecast information.</narrative>
  </description>
